Hi Simon, 

no I haven't, it's been on my mind, so thanks for prompting me.

Here is the data underlying this page: https://wwwspice/~ofrd-mopa/maremon/webpage/index.html
/data/users/ofrd-mopa/maremon/datasets/database_ofrd-mopa.csv

With a script to plot the NWS (Northwest European shelf), UKV (SSTs centred around the UK, domain run operationally), North Sea with MHW categories defined on 1982-2012: 
/home/users/segolene.berthou/workspace/ukep_plot/simple_plotting/marine_heatwave_ostiaTS_maremon.py

You can combine the "NRT" with "CDR" . CDR has undergone quality checks (goes up to June 2024), but not NRT (July 2024-now).

So I combine the two, e.g. 
ostia_cdr_NWS_sst and ostia_nrt_NWS_sst (replace nws by UKV or North_Sea)

But you can start with CDR. And with NWS.

Looking forward to discussing the results!
Ségolène
